<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Napoléon Louis Bonaparte</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1804">1804</a>–<a href="/years/1831">1831</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a> · Also known as Louis II of Holland</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Napoléon <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/louis-bonaparte">Louis Bonaparte</a> was the son of Louis Bonaparte, King of Holland, and Hortense de Beauharnais, and the elder brother of the future <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/napoleon-iii">Napoleon III</a>. Made Grand Duke of Berg as a small child in 1809, he was briefly proclaimed King of Holland as Louis II when his father abdicated in 1810. He died of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/measles">measles</a> in 1831 after joining a rising against the Papal States.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/napoleon-louis-bonaparte.jpg" alt="Napoléon Louis Bonaparte" width="320" height="414" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Thesupermat · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Napol%C3%A9on_III_et_l%27Italie_-_F%C3%A9lix_Cottrau_-_Le_prince_Napol%C3%A9on-Louis_Bonaparte_-_001.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
